# Cheeky Mouse sound circuits -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Vas Crabb's netlist of Cheeky Mouse's sound, with Couriersud's notes. Each 556 is declared
# one timer at a time as an NE555 (IC4_1, IC4_2 ...); they are written on the 556's pins
# here. The sound latch bits arrive as ports. VPLUS is the supply MAME approximates as
# 12.9V: its file says '15V dropped by three diodes and filtered'.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/universal/nl_cheekyms.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(cheekyms). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Vas Crabb (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/universal/nl_cheekyms.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
# The sheet numbers its ICs IC1, IC2 ...; they are written U1, U2 ... here, because the
# checker files every IC under a U designator.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 53: NET_C(I_V5.Q, IC1.11, IC1.13) -> nc -- 'shut the netlist parser up about unconnected inputs'
# MAME declares one section of these packages at a time; each is written on its package's
# pins by the data sheet's numbering of the sections (SECTION_PINS in the converter): U2 NE556 (IC2_1, IC2_2); U4 NE556 (IC4_1, IC4_2); U6 NE556 (IC6_1, IC6_2)
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): LOGIC_INPUT(I_MUTE), LOGIC_INPUT(I_CHEESE), LOGIC_INPUT(I_MUSIC), LOGIC_INPUT(I_MOUSE), LOGIC_INPUT(I_HAMMER), LOGIC_INPUT(I_PEST), LOGIC_INPUT(I_MOUSE_DIES), LOGIC_INPUT(I_PEST_DIES), LOGIC_INPUT(I_COIN_EXTRA)
#
# Not compared with the sheet: the site's one Cheeky Mouse schematic (doc 8bf94944bfe5,
# 'Main Block Diagram', drawing 8004) is the CPU and video board, and shows the sound board
# only as the connector pins it is wired to -- E1 (LS273) pins 2, 5, 6, 9, 12, 15, 16 and
# 19 and two of E2's go to it, and A7's coin pulse (read 2026-10-20). So two things here
# are assumptions, not readings: which timer of each 556 a sound uses (MAME's IC4_1 is
# taken as timer 1, pins 1-6, and IC4_2 as timer 2, pins 8-13; the sheet's own 556 at A7
# is numbered that way, which says nothing about the sound board's), and Q2's collector,
# which Couriersud's note says the schematic shows unconnected and this file leaves out.
#
# Not compared with the sheet. MAME's designators, values and pin numbers are taken as
# MAME has them; the checker shows the netlist is internally consistent (every pin exists,
# no two outputs fight, nothing floats), which is not the same as matching the board.

# part U1 7404
# part U2 NE556
# part U3 NE555
# part U4 NE556
# part U5 LM324
# part U6 NE556

value R1 10K
value R2 1M
value R3 1K
value R4 100K
value R5 1K
value R6 100K
value R7 1K
value R8 1M
value R9 10K
value R10 10K
value R11 10K
value R12 100K
value R13 100K
value R14 4.7K
value R15 1K
value R16 68K
value R17 100K
value R18 1K
value R19 150K
value R20 10K
value R21 100K
value R22 100K
value R23 1M
value R24 51K
value R25 20K
value R26 10K
value R27 220
value R28 100K
value R29 4.7K
value R30 1K
value R31 68K
value R32 100K
value R33 100K
value R34 51K
value R35 1M
value R36 1K
value R37 33K
value R38 560
value R39 100K
value R40 1K
value R41 47K
value R42 100K
value R43 10K
value R44 1K
value R45 47K
value R46 100K
value VR1 1K
value C8 0.1uF
value C9 0.1uF
value C10 10uF
value C11 0.1uF
value C12 0.01uF
value C13 10uF
value C14 0.01uF
value C15 0.01uF
value C16 0.1uF
value C17 2.2uF
value C18 10uF
value C19 0.01uF
value C20 0.22uF
value C21 0.01uF
value C22 47uF
value C23 0.033uF
value C24 0.01uF
value D4 1S1588
value D5 1S1588
value D6 1S1588
value D7 1S1588
value D8 1S1588
value D9 1S1588
value Q1 2SC945
value Q2 2SC945

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: C10.2 C12.2 C13.2 C14.2 C15.2 C16.2 C17.2 C18.2 C19.2 C20.2 C21.2 C22.2 C23.2 C24.2 U1.7 U3.1 U5.11 U2.7 U4.7 U6.7 Q1.E Q2.B R11.2 R4.2 R5.1 VR1.3
net +5V: U1.14 U3.4 U3.8 U5.4 U2.14 U4.14 U6.10 U6.14 U6.4 R15.1 R18.1 R23.1 R25.1 R29.1 R30.1 R35.2 R36.1 R40.1 R44.1 R9.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mute
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire U1.2 R1.1
wire C10.1 Q1.B R1.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cheese
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port VPLUS: R2.1  # in MAME: ANALOG_INPUT(I_VPLUS)
wire C8.1 Q2.E R2.2
wire C8.2 R3.1
wire U5.10 R3.2 R4.1
wire U5.9 R5.2 R6.1
wire C9.1 U5.8 R6.2
wire C9.2 R7.1
wire U5.13 R7.2 R8.1
wire C11.1 U5.14 R8.2
wire U1.4 R10.2
wire U5.12 R10.1 R9.1
wire C11.2 R11.1 R12.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mouse
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port MOUSE: D4.1 U4.4 R14.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_MOUSE)
wire C13.1 D4.2 U4.3 R14.2
wire U4.1 R15.2 R16.1
wire C12.1 U4.2 U4.6 R16.2
wire U4.5 R17.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hammer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire U6.1 R18.2 R19.1
wire C14.1 U6.2 U6.6 R19.2
wire U6.5 R20.1
wire C15.1 R20.2 R21.1
wire U5.6 R21.2 R22.1
wire U5.7 R22.2 R24.1
wire D5.1 U1.6
wire D5.2 D6.1
wire C16.1 D6.2 U5.5 R23.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pest
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire U3.7 R25.2 R26.1
wire C17.1 U3.2 U3.6 R26.2
wire U3.3 R27.1 R28.1
wire D7.1 R27.2
wire C18.1 D7.2 U6.11 R28.2 R29.2
wire U6.13 R30.2 R31.1
wire C19.1 U6.12 U6.8 R31.2
wire U6.9 R32.1
wire U5.2 R32.2 R33.1
wire U5.1 R33.2 R34.1
wire D8.1 U1.8
wire D8.2 D9.1
wire C20.1 D9.2 U5.3 R35.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mouse dies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port MOUSE_DIES: U2.10 R38.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_MOUSE_DIES)
wire C22.1 U2.11 R38.2
wire U2.13 R36.2 R37.1
wire C21.1 U2.12 U2.8 R37.2
wire U2.9 R39.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pest dies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire U2.1 R40.2 R41.1
wire C23.1 U2.2 U2.6 R41.2
wire U2.5 R42.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coin & extra
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire U4.13 R44.2 R45.1
wire C24.1 U4.12 U4.8 R45.2
wire U4.9 R46.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mixdown
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire Q1.C R12.2 R13.2 R17.2 R24.2 R34.2 R39.2 R42.2 R43.1
wire R43.2 R46.2 VR1.1
port MUTE: U1.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_MUTE)
port CHEESE: U1.3  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_CHEESE)
port MUSIC: R13.1  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_MUSIC)
port HAMMER: U1.5  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_HAMMER)
port PEST: U1.9  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_PEST)
port PEST_DIES: U2.4  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_PEST_DIES)
port COIN_EXTRA: U4.10  # in MAME: LOGIC_INPUT(I_COIN_EXTRA)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
nc U1.11 U1.13  # line 53: 'shut the netlist parser up about unconnected inputs'
# Pins the MAME netlist never mentions. On a real board these are unused outputs, or
# inputs left open or tied in a way MAME did not draw; they are written here so that
# the checker's coverage test still means something for every other pin.
nc U1.10 U1.12  # output output
nc U2.3  # CONT
nc U3.5  # CONT
nc U4.11  # CONT
nc U6.3  # CONT
